    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0567" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg497"/>

                <head>No. 290.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr.
                    West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 18,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to previous correspondence
                    concerning the incursions of British Indians into Montana Territory, I have the
                    honor to inclose herewith extracts from reports received by my colleague, the
                    Secretary of War, in regard to the recent hostile actions of a party of Cree
                    Indians, who invaded that Territory from Canada, and who escaped pursuit by
                    crossing the boundary.</p>
                <p>Requesting you to call the attention of the Canadian Government to this matter in
                    connection with my note of yesterday on the subject of Indian raids,</p>
                <p>1 have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>





                <xi:include href="d290-a1.xml" xpointer="d290-a1"/>
